    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Founded around 1336 by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sangama-dynasty">Sangama</a> brothers on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tungabhadra-river">Tungabhadra</a> as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi-sultanate">Delhi Sultanate</a> power collapsed in the south.</li><li>Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/krishnadevaraya">Krishnadevaraya</a> (r. 1509–1529) it was the dominant power of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, ruled from a vast capital at Hampi.</li><li>Defeat at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-talikota">Talikota</a> in 1565 led to the sack of the capital; nayaka governors became independent and the empire ended by 1646.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>The site of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chennai">Madras</a>, where the English built <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fort-st-george">Fort St George</a> in 1639–40, was granted by a local nayaka who served the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aravidu-dynasty">Aravidu</a> kings of Vijayanagara.</p></aside>
    </section>

